course: dictionary
lesson: 14434
title: Pacify: calm down or bring peace
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To pacify someone means to make them calm and quiet when they are angry or upset. Look at the clues: «Mum held the crying baby and sang softly until she pacified him.» The baby was crying, then he went quiet, so pacify means calm him down.
explain: Pacify can also mean to bring peace to a place, often by force, so that fighting there ends. «The army marched in to pacify the land.» The clue is that the fighting stopped, so here pacify means bring peace.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Could you say «Mum held the crying baby until she calmed him»? Yes, it still makes sense, so calm is the right meaning. Pacify is a verb, so it changes: pacify, pacifies, pacified, pacifying.
fact: Pacify is a verb: pacify, pacifies, pacified, pacifying.
fact: «Pacify» means to make an angry or upset person calm and quiet.
fact: «Pacify» can also mean to bring peace to a place, often by force, ending fighting there.
fact: In the USA, a baby's dummy is called a «pacifier».
fact: Phrases you may see: pacify a baby, try to pacify.
exercise: «The teacher tried to pacify the angry pupil.» What does pacify mean here? | To make the pupil angrier | *To make calm and quiet | To run away from the pupil | To shout loudly at the class
exercise: «The soldiers went to pacify the country by force, and the fighting stopped.» What does pacify mean here? | To make a loud noise | To count the people who live there | To paint the walls of the country | *To bring peace to a place and end fighting
exercise: In the USA, what is a baby's dummy called? | pacemaker | paperweight | packet | *pacifier
test: «Sam ___ his little sister, who had been crying, by reading her a story.» Which word fits? | pacify | pacifying | *pacified | pacifies
test: «Dad is ___ the angry customer by listening carefully.» Which word fits? | *pacifying | pacify | pacified | pacifies
exam: «The referee tried to pacify the angry crowd, and soon everyone was calm.» What does pacify mean? | To cheer the crowd on | To ask the crowd for money | *To calm down and make quiet | To start a riot
